      "status": "independently reviewed",
      "correspondence": "The first row of each minus minor has the same frame vector in every factor. A derivative paired against that row inserts one common column vector into a plus minor. Repeating in the same plus minor gives zero. In the other rows the proof bounds each box separately. The two-by-two differential example specializes the integer symbol algebra.",
      "review": "A second reader checked the definition, both directional derivatives, the limit of one distinguished-row differentiation per plus minor and the cap. Exact symbolic differentiation separately recovered Δ²G=0 and the specialized value −S."
    },
