      "title": "Integral contraction multiplicities and the coefficient bound",
      "anchor": "normalization-paired-valuation",
      "statement": "The (m,κ) coefficient of the product of the paired Laplacians applied to the symbol equals (∏ n_t!) times the integral contraction coefficient A. For a factorial-jet-integral residual series, norm |S|≤√p and |u_t|≤1, vanishing above the diagram caps and the ultrametric inequality give v_p≥−∑ C_t/2 for all output coefficients.",
