    {
      "id": "PMD-03",
      "chapter": "normalization",
      "title": "Passing from the diagram cap to the discriminant column valuation",
      "anchor": "normalization-paired-valuation",
      "statement": "In the actual chain the row conditions imply C_t≤cⱼ,ₜ at each word and step. At a used tuple and a level-free place above the discriminant prime d, the entry-to-lattice comparison then gives the uniform one-lift threshold −M_j/2−δ with a first-lift credit ηδ. Here M_j is the maximum over words of the sum of the row counts cⱼ,ₜ, and δ=v_p(DΓ) for the chosen word. Composition adds the thresholds to obtain the stated column bound on the ramified source lattice.",
      "dependencies": [
        "PMD-02",
        "THH-04"
      ],
